    "content": "U.S. Central Command (CENTCOM) is responsible for U.S. military operations in a 20-country area covering the Middle East, North Africa, and Central/South Asia. The region stretches across 4 million square miles, from Egypt to Pakistan and Kazakhstan to Yemen, including key maritime routes. CENTCOM Area of Responsibility (20 Nations): Levant/Middle East: Iraq, Israel, Jordan, Lebanon, Syria. Arabian Peninsula: Bahrain, Kuwait, Oman, Qatar, Saudi Arabia, United Arab Emirates (UAE), Yemen. Central Asia: Kazakhstan, Kyrgyzstan, Tajikistan, Turkmenistan, Uzbekistan. South Asia/Other: Afghanistan, Iran, Pakistan, Egypt. Note: While 20 countries fall directly under its area of responsibility, CENTCOM partners with a broader coalition for regional security.",
